{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghc1kUjMMy7KtLjWH3ur","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015omWXLukJQcNhcVfUQKazm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ar0_b0v5/NOTES.md","content":"# Parity of x[1], x[5], x[9], x[14]\n\nThe label depends only on s = x[1]+x[5]+x[9]+x[14], which is a whole number from 0 to 4.\n\n- **Layer 1:** Units 0–4 compute u_k = relu(s − k) for k = 0..4. All other units are zero.\n- **Layer 2:** Unit 0 computes f = u0 − 2u1 + 2u2 − 2u3 + 2u4. This is a piecewise-linear\n  \"zigzag\" that equals 0, 1, 0, 1, 0 at s = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, so f = parity(s). Because f ≥ 0,\n  the ReLU leaves it unchanged.\n- **Output:** logits = [0.5 − f, f − 0.5]. The argmax is class 1 exactly when f = 1.\n\nOn paper the network is exact for all 2^16 inputs. Every value it computes is a small\ninteger or a half-integer, so floating-point rounding is not a concern.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":533,"cache_read_input_tokens":5342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":533},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d346b6bb-df99-4531-9a2d-502348bcff21","uuid":"add69e5d-9645-4c31-a9e2-7fe3cd2aa922","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:52:56.895Z","request_id":"req_011Cghc1k8tyPXi2mJ11CtEc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015omWXLukJQcNhcVfUQKazm":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ar0_b0v5/NOTES.md","content":"# Parity of x[1], x[5], x[9], x[14]\n\nThe label depends only on s = x[1]+x[5]+x[9]+x[14], which is a whole number from 0 to 4.\n\n- **Layer 1:** Units 0–4 compute u_k = relu(s − k) for k = 0..4. All other units are zero.\n- **Layer 2:** Unit 0 computes f = u0 − 2u1 + 2u2 − 2u3 + 2u4. This is a piecewise-linear\n  \"zigzag\" that equals 0, 1, 0, 1, 0 at s = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, so f = parity(s). Because f ≥ 0,\n  the ReLU leaves it unchanged.\n- **Output:** logits = [0.5 − f, f − 0.5]. The argmax is class 1 exactly when f = 1.\n\nOn paper the network is exact for all 2^16 inputs. Every value it computes is a small\ninteger or a half-integer, so floating-point rounding is not a concern.\n"}}}
